      <room>H.1302</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>The difficulty of forking</title>
      <subtitle>and why you should not do it, yet prepare for it</subtitle>
      <track>CrossDistro devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Forking a project is never an easy task both on social and technical level.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Mageia, like Libreoffice, is a big project born from a fork, and faced several issues regarding community and infrastructure. The lessons learned from forking can be generalized to any software project.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="731">Anne Nicolas</person>
          <person id="732">Michael Scherer</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>